    脓 | nóng | pus
    哝 | nóng | mutter; murmur softly
    曆 | lì | calendar; almanac
    歷 | lì | experience; pass through

semantic_boundary_contrasts:
  core_nuance: 农历 specifically designates China's traditional lunisolar calendar that synchronizes lunar phases with agricultural solar terms.
  contrasts[3]{id,compared_word,pinyin,analysis}:
    1 | 农历 vs. 公历 | gōnglì | 农历 is the traditional Chinese lunisolar calendar used for agrarian cycles and ancestral festivals, whereas 公历 is the internationally standard Gregorian solar calendar used for civil administration and modern commerce.
    2 | 农历 vs. 阴历 | yīnlì | 农历 is strictly a lunisolar calendar incorporating 24 solar terms to reflect solar cycles, while 阴历 colloquially refers to lunar reckoning, though in strict astronomy 阴历 relies solely on lunar moon phases without solar adjustments.
    3 | 农历 vs. 日历 | rìlì | 农历 refers to the cultural calendar system itself, whereas 日历 denotes the physical calendar booklet, wall chart, or digital schedule application displaying day-to-day dates.

extended_reading_passages[2]{id,hanzi,pinyin,en,es}:
  #1 | 每当翻开传统的农历，四季更迭的节律总会唤醒深层的乡愁。春耕夏耘，秋收冬藏，我们在月圆月缺间体悟生命的丰盈。农历不仅记录着岁月，更寄托着千家万户对团聚的永恒期盼。 | Měi dāng fānkāi chuántǒng de nónglì, sìjì gēngdié de jiélǜ zǒng huì huànxǐng shēncéng de xiāngchóu. Chūngēng xiàyún, qiūshōu dōngcáng, wǒmen zài yuèyuán yuèquē jiān tǐwù shēngmìng de fēngyíng. Nónglì bùjǐn jìlù zhe suìyuè, gèng jìtuō zhe qiānjiā-wànhù duì tuánjù de yǒnghéng qīpàn. | Whenever opening the traditional lunar calendar, the rhythms of shifting seasons awaken deep nostalgic longings. Sowing in spring and storing in winter, we perceive the richness of life between waxing and waning moons. The agricultural calendar not only marks passing years, but cradles eternal hopes of reunion. | Cada vez que se abre el calendario lunar tradicional, el compás de las cuatro estaciones despierta una honda nostalgia. Entre siembras primaverales y cosechas otoñales, contemplamos la plenitud de la vida. Este calendario no solo registra el tiempo, sino el anhelo perenne de reencuentro familiar.
  #2 | 农历是中国古代天文学与农业实践高度融合的智慧结晶，精准协调了太阳与月亮的运行周期。二十四节气被列入人类非物质文化遗产名录，标志着以农历为载体的东方自然生态观获得了国际社会的广泛认同。 | Nónglì shì Zhōngguó gǔdài tiānwénxué yǔ nóngyè shíjiàn gāodù rónghé de zhìhuì jiéjīng, jīngzhǔn xiétiáo le tàiyáng yǔ yuèliang de yùnxíng zhōuqī. Èrshísì jiéqì bèi lièrù rénlèi fēiwùzhì wénhuà yíchǎn mínglù, biāozhì zhe yǐ nónglì wéi zàitǐ de dōngfāng zìrán shēngtàiguān huòdé le guójì shèhuì de guǎnfàn rèntóng. | The lunar calendar is the crystalline culmination of ancient Chinese astronomy and farming, harmonizing the cycles of the sun and moon. The inclusion of the 24 Solar Terms on UNESCO's Intangible Cultural Heritage list marks global recognition of the ecological worldview embodied by this calendar. | El calendario tradicional es la cristalización del saber astronómico y agrícola chino, armonizando los ciclos solares y lunares. La inscripción de los 24 Periodos Solares en la lista del Patrimonio Inmaterial de la UNESCO ratifica el reconocimiento mundial de su cosmovisión ecológica.